{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"cdccdde7-d803-4eb8-909c-fb72f7dfd4ef","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Start with a golden rectangle. Removing its largest square leaves a smaller golden rectangle, rotated ninety degrees. Lengths shown are rounded.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Golden spiral from nested squares"},{"op":"equation","id":"ratio","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\varphi=\\frac{1+\\sqrt5}{2}\\approx1.618"},{"op":"figure","id":"construction","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.6,8.7],"y":[-0.6,5.6],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"polyline","id":"rectangle","points":[[0,0],[8.09,0],[8.09,5],[0,5]],"closed":true},{"kind":"segment","id":"first_cut","from":[5,0],"to":[5,5]},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,-0.3],"to":[8.09,-0.3],"label":"8.09"},{"kind":"measure","from":[-0.3,0],"to":[-0.3,5],"label":"5"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"cdccdde7-d803-4eb8-909c-fb72f7dfd4ef","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Keep removing the largest square. Inside each square, draw a quarter-circle; successive arcs meet smoothly as their radii shrink.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"large_arcs","on":"construction","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":[5,1.91],"to":[8.09,1.91]},{"kind":"segment","from":[6.18,0],"to":[6.18,1.91]},{"kind":"arc","center":[5,0],"r":5,"start":90,"end":180},{"kind":"arc","center":[5,1.91],"r":3.09,"start":0,"end":90},{"kind":"arc","center":[6.18,1.91],"r":1.91,"start":-90,"end":0}]},{"op":"equation","id":"sizes","anchor":{"el":"ratio","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"5,\\quad3.09,\\quad1.91,\\quad1.18,\\quad\\ldots"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"cdccdde7-d803-4eb8-909c-fb72f7dfd4ef","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The construction repeats inward. Each new square has side length divided by the golden ratio, so each quarter-circle shrinks by that same factor.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"small_arcs","on":"construction","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":[5,1.18],"to":[6.18,1.18]},{"kind":"segment","from":[5.73,1.18],"to":[5.73,1.91]},{"kind":"arc","center":[6.18,1.18],"r":1.18,"start":-180,"end":-90},{"kind":"arc","center":[5.73,1.18],"r":0.73,"start":90,"end":180}]},{"op":"equation","id":"shrink","anchor":{"el":"sizes","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"s_{n+1}=\\frac{s_n}{\\varphi}"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"By what factor does the square's side shrink at each stage?","expected_gist":"Divide by φ, or multiply by about 0.618."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"cdccdde7-d803-4eb8-909c-fb72f7dfd4ef","step":{"id":"s4","script":"These circular arcs approximate a golden spiral. The exact spiral is logarithmic: its radius grows by the golden ratio every quarter-turn outward.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"approximation","anchor":{"el":"shrink","side":"below","gap":0.1},"content":"Quarter-circles: an approximation"},{"op":"equation","id":"exact_spiral","anchor":{"el":"approximation","side":"below","gap":0.07},"latex":"r(\\theta)=a\\varphi^{2\\theta/\\pi},\\qquad a>0"},{"op":"equation","id":"growth","anchor":{"el":"exact_spiral","side":"below","gap":0.07},"latex":"r\\!\\left(\\theta+\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)=\\varphi\\,r(\\theta)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
